    <br>
    Sorry, but that doesn't directly follow.  <br>
    <br>
    With visible content type, an observer can *trivially* tell apart
    the two flows you mentioned in your next message.  With current
    stacks' (lack of) padding and timing obfuscation, the observer can
    still tell the flows apart ... but you have a chance of writing a
    stack that prevents the observer from doing so.  I don't think that
    "goes from 'impossible' to 'you have to write code'" can be
    construed as exactly zero benefit.<br>
